&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re the world&#39;s leading consumer healthcare platform, supporting millions of patients across the US, Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan, Spain and Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re driven by the belief that good health should last a lifetime, and that to get there we need to deliver the personalised, high quality and empathetic care that the traditional system cannot support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner with our care teams of prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists and dietitians to support patients across preventative health, weight management and specific women&#39;s and men&#39;s health conditions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We joined Hims &amp;amp; Hers so that you can do all of the above on a bigger scale, with more ambition, a stronger global brand and the resources to deliver care to patients in dozens of countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for people who appreciate and are excited by the enormity and uniqueness of this challenge, and want to work in the most ambitious, smart, fast moving and positive sum environment of their lives to transform how healthcare is delivered globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We hope that&#39;s you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager, you will lead an engineering team to ensure fast, high-quality execution. You will focus on rapid experimentation and technical excellence across the full customer lifecycle - from awareness and acquisition through to retention, revenue, and referral.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Engineering Manager, you’ll lead or more small squads, typically our teams consist of 3-4 engineers working alongside a product manager and a designer. Each squad owns its problem area and its OKRs end to end, with very little red tape. We ship hundreds of times a month, merged code is live in minutes, and growth experiments read out in weeks, so you’ll quickly see what your team’s work does for patients and for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering here is deliberately lean, which means every leader has real influence over what gets built and how, and progression means more ownership, not just a bigger team. You’ll stay close to the architecture and technical decisions, working with senior engineers who value someone who can challenge a design and keep the team moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating at the intersection of engineering, product, and growth marketing, you will partner with cross-functional stakeholders to translate strategic visions into scalable engineering solutions. You will be responsible for empowering your team, optimising execution velocity, and maintaining high engineering standards as we scale our preventative care ecosystem globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure High-Quality Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage an engineering team or function to drive fast, reliable software delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resolve Technical &amp;amp; Operational Blockers:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as an escalation point for complex technical and operational issues, solving them efficiently to keep projects on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimise Workloads:&lt;/strong&gt; Balance priorities and take active responsibility for optimising team workload to maintain predictable delivery without burnout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Growth &amp;amp; Experimentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the execution of sophisticated, data-driven experiments and growth initiatives across the entire patient journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve Engineering Processes:&lt;/strong&gt; Continuously refine development processes, workflows, and team structures to build a high-velocity environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build &amp;amp; Mentor Talent:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with talent acquisition teams to recruit, onboard, and retain world-class engineers while fostering a culture of ownership, psychological safety, and high morale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Align Cross-Functionally&lt;/strong&gt; : Partner seamlessly with Product, Marketing, and Data stakeholders to align technical delivery with commercial goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Strength &amp;amp; Codebase Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; You are technically strong and partner credibly with senior engineers-able to evaluate system architecture and spot when technical estimates lack substance. Coding is not the primary job, but you are comfortable getting on the tools in an ecosystem built on React, React Native, TypeScript, Go microservices, GraphQL, Kubernetes, and GCP, and delivering work to unblock your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record leading an engineering team to ensure fast and high-quality execution. First-time managers are welcome!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Focus:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated capability in solving escalated issues, optimising team workloads, and driving continuous improvements across team workflows and structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimentation &amp;amp; Growth Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on background or strong familiarity with rapid experimentation, A/B testing, and building software optimised for user engagement, conversion, and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People-First Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled at mentoring engineers, navigating shifting priorities, and nurturing an inclusive, highly motivated team culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional communication skills with a history of bridging technical delivery with product strategy, growth marketing, and commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in regulated sectors (such as healthtech, fintech or gaming), finding creative paths forward inside compliance constraints rather than being stopped by them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why join Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s next&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Our goal for the next three years is to support 1 million patients globally to live better for longer, launching into new conditions, demographics and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build something world-changing&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- We&#39;re on the path to becoming the world&#39;s largest international digital healthcare company. It will be challenging, fast-paced and deeply rewarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make real impact&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Your work directly shapes patient outcomes and scales evidence-based care across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate your growth&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- High ownership, continuous feedback and dedicated development support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join a motivated team&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Talented peers solving complex clinical and operational problems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What&#39;s ahead in the UK&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be an owner&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Your own stake in the business with our employee options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invest in your growth&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Annual development budget plus 3 days of professional development leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work flexibly&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Hybrid setup with 3 days a week in our Old Street office, designed for focus and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your well-being&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Private health insurance through Vitality, or a monthly wellness allowance to spend on what matters most to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take time off&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- 25 days of holiday, enhanced parental leave and work from anywhere 3 weeks a year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join a connected team&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- A vibrant office culture with regular socials, clubs, after-school sport and seasonal events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;📍London/ UK remote | 💰 &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/documents/engineering-progression-framework-v4-1.pdf&quot;&gt;Engineer III&lt;/a&gt; £78,000 - £110,000 base salary per year ➕ share options | &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers/&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/technology&quot;&gt;Technology&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our Mobile Engineering discipline&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our mobile engineers have a variety of different backgrounds&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are ~60 iOS engineers at Monzo and we’re looking for more to join the team. We have several non-graduates; only some of us studied Computer Science; some of us have worked in huge companies; some have only ever worked in startups; others are former consultants. As long as you enjoy learning new things, we’d love to talk to you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monzo works in small, interdisciplinary teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have around 650 engineers out of roughly 5,500 people in total - and we have big ambitions. There are many interesting challenges ahead, and we&#39;re happy for people to move between teams or to specialise, whatever you prefer. As an engineer here you&#39;d be able to work directly with anyone across the company, and we run regular knowledge-sharing sessions so you’ll learn heaps about everything from how banks work to effective communication.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We contribute to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/monzo&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;open source software&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; as much as possible. Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/technology&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;blog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;is a good place to learn even more about what we do!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your day-to-day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re searching for &lt;strong&gt;product-focused iOS engineers&lt;/strong&gt; to evolve our native mobile app.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;You’ll take pride in building polished user experiences, and you’ll balance the need for well-tested resilient code with moving fast and iterating.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be working on a product that is a part of day to day life for more than 15 million people already, and your work here will shape the way that people interact with their finances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an iOS Engineer at Monzo you&#39;ll work in a small, autonomous product squad alongside Android Engineers, Backend Engineers, User Researchers, Product Designers, Product Managers, QA Testers, and Data Scientists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You and your team will be responsible for an overall company goal, rather than building a specific feature - you&#39;ll have the opportunity to have impact on both &lt;em&gt;what&lt;/em&gt; we build, and &lt;em&gt;how&lt;/em&gt; we build it. Mobile engineers at Monzo work on everything from the personal banking product to customer support tools. We also have a small mobile platform squad dedicated to enabling other engineers to move faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every week we meet as an iOS discipline to discuss tools, techniques, problems we&#39;re encountering across the company and work together to improve our codebase and processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to an engineering manager who will meet with you every 1-2 weeks 1:1. They’re dedicated to helping you grow and develop as an engineer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our iOS app&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our app is 100% &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.swift.org/&quot;&gt;Swift&lt;/a&gt; and our latest features are built in &lt;a href=&quot;https://developer.apple.com/tutorials/swiftui/&quot;&gt;SwiftUI&lt;/a&gt; and using elements of &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/pointfreeco/swift-composable-architecture&quot;&gt;The Composable Architecture&lt;/a&gt;. Historically we built using a Model, View, View-Model architecture (MVVM). We use Coordinators to ensure we can re-use flows wherever possible, and avoid tightly coupling one screen to another. We make heavy use of protocols and extensions throughout our app.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our networking stack is built upon &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Alamofire/Alamofire&quot;&gt;Alamofire&lt;/a&gt;, using a generic interface to easily de-serialise objects of a certain type, and we mirror our backend micro-service architecture by building individual services to house our API logic. We log liberally to get alerted when they’re triggered in &lt;a href=&quot;https://sentry.io/welcome/&quot;&gt;Sentry&lt;/a&gt; which we also use to monitor crashes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our testing stack comprises of unit tests for business logic, stubbed API tests for pseudo-integration tests, snapshot tests for UI, and XCUITest for testing user input and sequencing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;ve published some talks and blog posts about how we work:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/2017/07/07/working-with-backend-services-on-ios/&quot;&gt;Working with backend services on iOS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jDvk7nztqHw&quot;&gt;Pushing Protocols to their Limits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/2022/06/23/our-mobile-release-process-an-illustrated-story&quot;&gt;Our mobile release process: An illustrated story&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.leedsmobile.com/past-talks#h.pxrhbkspk22g&quot;&gt;What we’ve learnt building a design system in SwiftUI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You should apply if&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about the impact your work has on our customers, and optimise for outcomes rather than the number of lines of code you output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited about and have experience in programming in Swift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve shipped and iterated on at least one app in the App Store&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a product mindset: you care about customer outcomes and you want to make data-informed decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love turning excellent design into beautiful products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable working in a team that deals with ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an understanding computer science principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Interview Process&lt;/h3&gt;
